# The nightly service's direct dependencies, pinned exactly; `make lock`
# compiles them into requirements-service.txt with hashes, which the image and
# CI install. The newest set that works together (2026-10-02): statsforecast
# 2.1.1 requires pandas below 3, and pandas 2.3 under numpy 2.5 warns on every
# date sum that numpy will later refuse, so numpy stays on 2.4.
# The nightly service's image. Deliberately WITHOUT the gradient boosters: the
# per-product model they serve has been off by default since it forecast
# October, the best month of the year, at a quarter of what October has ever
# been. They were two thirds of the image and were being imported on every run
# for nothing. Switching FORECAST_M5 back on needs requirements-m5.txt as well.
numpy==2.4.6
pandas==2.3.3
openpyxl==3.1.5
# scipy: the non-negative least squares behind the blend weights, and the floor
# statsmodels and statsforecast both stand on.
scipy==1.18.1
# Holt-Winters and the simple exponential smoothing behind Theta.
statsmodels==0.15.0
# More voices for the panel: AutoETS, AutoARIMA, AutoTheta, AutoCES. Optional
# at runtime - simple.py skips them when the import fails.
statsforecast==2.1.1
